mill-proof.logic.r1: argue/equivocates: P3 (S6): it takes "desirable" from capable of being desired, which actual desire proves (S3) to worth desiring, a good (S6), a reader says: the argument holds only through it; without it, C1 (S6) does not follow (mill-proof.logic.r1.sense1)
mill-proof.logic.r1: argue/countermodel: C1 (S6): desired_own = T, good_own = F
